3	 * right element type; does aria-checked/tabIndex track isSelected/isFocusable; does the passed
4	 * imageUrl reach the DOM as the swatch's background-image fill; and — the regression guard —
5	 * does the swatch box's background-colour stay pinned to the recipe's own token declaration
6	 * regardless of the colour `name`, rather than picking up a raw CSS-colour-keyword the way base
7	 * SFCC's own `renderDefaultVariationAttribute` does (`backgroundColor={name.toLowerCase()}`) —
8	 * see index.tsx's own comment for the three reasons this atom deliberately does not replicate
9	 * that.
10	 *
11	 * Every render needs three wrappers, not just the router:
12	 *   - `ChakraProvider theme={theme}` (the real theme, not Chakra's default) — without it,
13	 *     `useMultiStyleConfig('ZimmColourSwatch', ...)` resolves against a theme with no such key
14	 *     registered and silently returns `{}` for both parts, which would make every assertion below
15	 *     pass vacuously against an unstyled node rather than against this recipe. Same reasoning as
16	 *     zimmProductMeta/index.test.tsx's own "resolves its recipe under a ChakraProvider" test.
17	 *   - `MemoryRouter` — this atom can render a react-router `Link`, which throws outside one.
18	 *   - `ZimmTokensGlobal` — without a `:root` definition for the `--zimm-*` variables the recipe
19	 *     references, a resolved-value assertion has nothing to distinguish "correct" from
20	 *     "regressed" (see the regression-guard test below).
21	 *
22	 * `getComputedStyle`, not `element.style`: Chakra resolves `__css` through Emotion, which applies
23	 * a generated class rather than an inline `style` attribute, so the inline `style` property never
24	 * reflects the resolved value — matching how every other Chakra-styles assertion in this codebase
25	 * reads a resolved value (zimmProductMeta/index.test.tsx, zimmProductPrice/index.test.tsx,
26	 * theme/index.test.tsx).
27	 *
28	 * One further, load-bearing wrinkle specific to a `var(--zimm-*)`-driven recipe (as opposed to a
29	 * bare Chakra-scale key, which those other files' assertions read): confirmed directly against
30	 * this file, jsdom's `getComputedStyle` does not substitute a custom property's value — it
31	 * echoes back the literal declaration text (`"var(--zimm-color-bg-02)"`), never the
32	 * resolved hex/rgb. That is actually what makes the regression guard below simple rather than
33	 * impossible: it asserts on that literal, unsubstituted declaration string, which is exactly
34	 * "which value authored this" — variable reference vs. some other literal. A real browser (Chrome
35	 * driving the Storybook `play` in index.stories.tsx) does perform the substitution; this file
36	 * doesn't need it to, because the literal declaration is the more direct thing to assert on.
37	 *
38	 * No ZimmIcon anywhere in this component, so no need for the ZimmIcon-throws-under-Vitest mock
39	 * documented in testing.md.
40	 */
